---
description: ReverbScope execution standard for every session
alwaysApply: true
---

The execution standard is `docs/GUIDELINES.zh-CN.md` (v2.1.1).
`docs/GUIDELINES.md` is an English summary. `AGENTS.md` is the working copy
of Appendix J. If these files disagree, the Chinese guidelines win.

Before editing, read guidelines §0, §2, §3, §4, §6, and Appendix J, plus the
sections the task names. One task, one branch, one pull request. Do not open
a second full GUI redesign. Do not commit on `main`, `release/0.5.0`, or
`gui/redesign`.

Do not change `core/`, `models/`, `interpretation/`, `health.py`, file
formats, CLI output, dependencies, `.github/`, or the license unless that is
the task. Stop and ask when the task conflicts with the guidelines.

Do not merge, publish, tag, close a pull request, force-push, or delete a
remote branch. Do not delete or weaken a test to go green. Do not edit the
guidelines or their version number.

Name the evidence level. Hardware or DAW is above CI, the fake backend, and
offscreen screenshots, which are above a synthetic demo. Unrun checks are
"not run". Never write an email address, an OpenAI organization id, or a
token into the tree, a commit, or a pull request.

Commit messages end with `Assisted-by:`. The pull request ends with the
Appendix J handoff, in Chinese for the maintainer, and stays a draft until
the maintainer reviews it.
